From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Paul Praschl <praschlpaul@g-p.at>
Date: Mon, 27 Jul 2026 10:22:52 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 050/117] dt-bindings: serial: samsung: add Apple T8010 UART

The T8010 UART block uses the Apple S5L register layout, but it needs
SoC-specific match data for baud-rate programming.

Add an apple,t8010-uart compatible so the driver can select that data.
Keep apple,s5l-uart as the fallback for the common register interface and
existing S5L compatibility.

Signed-off-by: Paul Praschl <praschlpaul@g-p.at>

Orchard-replay-of: cb92ff2bc4cb96774fe8ad81ddb0fdff89050e0e
---
 Documentation/devicetree/bindings/serial/samsung_uart.yaml | 6 ++++--
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/serial/samsung_uart.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/serial/samsung_uart.yaml
index 75ac2a08f..df763d5ae 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/serial/samsung_uart.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/serial/samsung_uart.yaml
@@ -29,8 +29,10 @@ properties:
           - samsung,exynos850-uart
           - samsung,exynos8895-uart
       - items:
-          - enum:
-              - samsung,exynos2200-uart
+          - const: apple,t8010-uart
+          - const: apple,s5l-uart
+      - items:
+          - const: samsung,exynos2200-uart
           - const: google,gs101-uart
       - items:
           - enum:
